{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And YHWH remembered Sarah, etc.</b> Scripture placed this passage adjacent to teach you that everyone who seeks mercy for his fellow and he himself needs that same thing — he is answered first (Bava Kamma 92), as it says ״וַיִּתְפַּלֵּל״, etc., and adjacent to it ״and YHWH remembered Sarah״ — that she was remembered already before he healed Avimelech." "<b>remembered Sarah as He had said.</b> In conception." "<b>as He had spoken.</b> In birth. And where is the 'saying', and where is the 'speaking'? The 'saying' — ״וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים אֲבָל שָׂרָה אִשְׁתְּךָ״, etc. (Genesis 17). The 'speaking' was the word of YHWH to Avram in the covenant between the pieces, and there it says ״לֹא יִירָשְׁךָ זֶה״, etc. (ibid. 15) — and He will bring the heir from her." "<b>And YHWH did for Sarah as He had spoken.</b> To Avraham."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:42.908578089Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}